I have the usable fact table and flight-leg fields. Next I’m building the itinerary rollup by `FlightDate + TailNum + FlightNum + Carrier`, then deduplicating by full `Route` so the dashboard returns the 10 most recent unique highest-hop patterns.
tool altinity_ontime_demo.execute_query({"query":"WITH itineraries AS (\n    SELECT\n        FlightDate,\n        TailNum AS aircraft_id,\n        FlightNum AS flight_number,\n        Carrier AS carrier,\n        arraySort(x -> x.1, groupArray((coalesce(DepTime, CRSDepTime, toUInt16(0)), OriginCode, DestCode))) AS legs\n    FROM ontime.fact_ontime\n    WHERE Cancelled = 0\n      AND TailNum != ''\n      AND FlightNum != ''\n    GROUP BY FlightDate, aircraft_id, flight_number, carrier\n    HAVING count() > 1\n)\nSELECT\n    FlightDate,\n    aircraft_id,\n    flight_number,\n    carrier,\n    length(legs) AS hop_count,\n    arrayStringConcat(arrayMap(x -> x.2, legs), '-') || '-' || arrayElement(legs, -1).3 AS Route\nFROM itineraries\nORDER BY hop_count DESC, FlightDate DESC\nLIMIT 10","limit":50})
